# Globs ADDED to the governed set, one per line.
#
# `check_records.py` governs every Markdown file that carries `record_type:` frontmatter -- that is
# the selection. This file only ADDS paths to it: a record you want graded even if its frontmatter
# goes missing. To take a file OUT, name it in `.governed-records-exempt` with a reason.
#
# A glob written from memory once matched nothing, so the rules it was meant to switch on stayed off
# while the file looked like a working control. Every glob below is checked against the paths the
# Makefile and AGENTS.md say the workflow writes, by `conformance/test-governed-paths.py`.
docs/decisions.md
docs/closure-report-*.md
docs/plans/m*-wave-*-close.md
# M11-W1. Added by the independent seat's BLOCKING-2: 44 files under `docs/reviews/` carried
# `record_type: review` and NONE of them was ever scanned, because this file never named them.
# The line above says it plainly -- "delete a line and you are choosing to leave those records
# ungoverned" -- and nobody had chosen; the directory simply never got a line. D-133 makes a
# review record load-bearing (a wave closes green on what its `seat:` says), so an ungoverned
# review is now an unchecked dependency of every wave close.
#
# SCOPED BY ERA, and the scope is a decision rather than an accident. `docs/reviews/*.md` produced
# 30 findings, every one of them in an M1-M7 record and none in M8 or later: 27 files predate
# frontmatter entirely and 3 carry a `status:` value the flow no longer has. GPF-001 already ruled
# that a tool may not retroactively invalidate records written before it existed, so the glob names
# M8 onward -- the era in which a review record became load-bearing. The pre-M8 reviews are
# out of scope and are NOT silently fine; they are unparsed prose, and that is what they were.
#
# A review that is cited by a wave close and matches none of these globs is still not free: D-133's
# gate reads `seat:` out of the cited record's FRONTMATTER, so a wave cannot close green on a review
# this manifest does not reach.
docs/reviews/m8-*.md
docs/reviews/m9-*.md
docs/reviews/m1[0-9]-*.md
docs/fixpack-*.md
docs/EXPERIENCE.md
# M14 closure seat, MINOR. `docs/research/` was ungoverned and M14 put a record there; the seat
# gave that file a bogus `record_type`, a duplicate `id` and a bogus `status`, and the gate still
# reported PASS. A directory nobody named is W-012's shape, and a research record is cited by a
# plan the owner rules from.
# DevFlow v6.0 (D-155): governance is now derived from `record_type:` frontmatter, so every research
# record is governed whatever this file says; the glob is narrowed to the record SHAPE the directory
# uses (`<topic>-<date>.md` and `m<N>-<topic>.md`), which `test-governed-paths.py` requires.
docs/research/*-20[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9].md
docs/research/m[0-9]*-*.md
